WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.032 --> 00:00:12.372
Several weeks passed.

2
00:00:13.473 --> 00:00:16.654
One morning Mowgli climbed onto Rama's back.

3
00:00:17.754 --> 00:00:20.836
Rama was the largest male in the herd of buffalo.

4
00:00:21.616 --> 00:00:23.917
The other animals began following Rama.

5
00:00:29.419 --> 00:00:33.185
the cattle on your own today," Mowgli said to the other children.

6
00:00:33.205 --> 00:00:35.905
"I'm going to stay with the buffalo."

7
00:00:38.566 --> 00:00:41.307
Mowgli led the buffalo to the edge of the plain.

8
00:00:42.287 --> 00:00:44.588
That was where the river came out of the jungle.

9
00:00:45.448 --> 00:00:49.669
Then he dropped off Rama's back and ran toward the bamboo.

10
00:00:50.309 --> 00:00:53.650
Gray Brother was waiting there, just as Mowgli had hoped.

11
00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:56.331
They greeted one another happily.

12
00:00:57.931 --> 00:00:59.752
But Gray Brother looked worried.

13
00:01:01.616 --> 00:01:04.517
"Shere Khan came back to the jungle to wait for you.

14
00:01:05.578 --> 00:01:07.519
There was little food, so he left.

15
00:01:08.879 --> 00:01:10.560
He will come back soon, Mowgli.

16
00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:13.581
And this time he will kill you."

17
00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:21.305
"When the tiger returns, wait for me in the ravine near the flowering tree."

18
00:01:22.105 --> 00:01:24.586
Mowgli pointed to a rock across the plain.

19
00:01:24.606 --> 00:01:28.648
"Until then, sit on that rock, where I can see you."

20
00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:35.533
Every day Mowgli herded the buffalo.

21
00:01:36.353 --> 00:01:40.994
Day after day he saw Gray Brother sitting on the rock across the plain.

22
00:01:41.894 --> 00:01:48.096
Most days Mowgli just lay on the grass, listening carefully to the sounds as Father Wolf had taught

23
00:01:48.136 --> 00:01:53.878
him. If Shere Khan approached, Mowgli would surely hear him in the stillness.

24
00:01:56.238 --> 00:01:58.519
One day Mowgli glanced at the rock.

25
00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:01.300
It was empty.

26
00:02:03.232 --> 00:02:07.414
Quickly he herded the buffalo to the tree with the golden red flowers.

27
00:02:10.615 --> 00:02:12.016
There sat Gray Brother.

28
00:02:13.396 --> 00:02:15.577
Every hair on his back was standing up.

29
00:02:16.578 --> 00:02:20.259
"Shere Khan has been hiding for a month," Gray Brother said.

30
00:02:20.279 --> 00:02:24.681
"But last night he crossed the plains with Tabaqui."

31
00:02:25.541 --> 00:02:26.502
Mowgli frowned.

32
00:02:26.522 --> 00:02:31.003
"Tabaqui?" Mowgli was not afraid of Shere Khan.

33
00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:34.494
However, Tabaqui was another story.

34
00:02:35.474 --> 00:02:37.376
The jackal was very cunning.

35
00:02:37.396 --> 00:02:39.497
"Have no fear.

36
00:02:40.458 --> 00:02:43.680
I met Tabaqui at dawn—and took care of him."

37
00:02:44.381 --> 00:02:46.022
Gray Brother licked his lips.

38
00:02:46.042 --> 00:02:51.646
"First he gave me some important information.

39
00:02:52.447 --> 00:02:55.769
Shere Khan plans to wait for you at the village gate tonight."

40
00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:58.491
"Where's Shere Khan now?"

41
00:02:58.931 --> 00:02:59.752
Mowgli asked.

42
00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.121
"He's in the big, dry ravine.

43
00:03:03.481 --> 00:03:04.642
The one along the river."

44
00:03:04.662 --> 00:03:07.664
"Has he hunted yet today?"

45
00:03:08.184 --> 00:03:09.005
Mowgli asked.

46
00:03:09.565 --> 00:03:12.387
The answer could mean his own life or death.

47
00:03:12.407 --> 00:03:17.150
"He ate a large meal at dawn," Gray Brother replied.

48
00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:20.511
"Good." Mowgli was thinking aloud.

49
00:03:21.632 --> 00:03:24.294
"That means he'll be too full to move fast.

50
00:03:25.294 --> 00:03:27.796
If there were more of us, we could attack him.

51
00:03:29.688 --> 00:03:33.090
But these buffalo will not charge unless they smell him.

52
00:03:34.151 --> 00:03:37.874
And I cannot speak their language yet to explain things to them.

53
00:03:38.854 --> 00:03:41.316
Do you think we can pick up the tiger's scent?

54
00:03:42.117 --> 00:03:44.138
That way the buffalo can smell it."

55
00:03:45.139 --> 00:03:46.620
Gray Brother shook his head.

56
00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:49.582
"Shere Khan traveled in the river.

57
00:03:50.002 --> 00:03:51.243
This leaves no scent."

58
00:03:52.704 --> 00:03:54.986
"Tabaqui must have told him to do that.

59
00:03:55.946 --> 00:03:58.188
Shere Khan would not have thought of it alone."

60
00:03:59.652 --> 00:04:01.953
Mowgli stood with his finger in his mouth.

61
00:04:01.973 --> 00:04:08.697
"I can take the buffalo through the jungle to the head of the ravine.

62
00:04:09.778 --> 00:04:13.900
We can block that end but Shere Khan will escape the other way.

63
00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:16.661
We must block the other end too."

64
00:04:18.542 --> 00:04:19.783
Mowgli looked at the wolf.

65
00:04:19.803 --> 00:04:23.545
"Can you take half of the animals and do that?"

66
00:04:25.186 --> 00:04:29.328
"Not by myself, but I have brought a wise helper."

67
00:04:30.432 --> 00:04:33.214
Gray Brother ran off and dropped into a hole.

68
00:04:34.775 --> 00:04:37.357
Seconds later a gray head popped up.

69
00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:41.620
The hot air filled with a familiar hunting howl.

70
00:04:42.921 --> 00:04:44.963
Mowgli clapped his hands in delight.
